% High Frequency Chest Wall Oscillation Devices: LCD L33785 and its Policy
% Article A52494 (DME MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it
% includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need,
% refills) and states when a claim for a high frequency chest wall
% oscillation device (E0483) or a replacement vest or hose used with
% beneficiary owned equipment (A7025, A7026) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY:
% one of the three diagnosis criteria — cystic fibrosis; bronchiectasis
% confirmed by a CT scan with a daily productive cough of six months or
% frequent exacerbations needing antibiotics; one of the named neuromuscular
% diseases — and the well-documented failure of standard treatments to
% mobilize retained secretions; and not the concurrent use of a mechanical
% in-exsufflation device (E0482).
%
% How the criteria are read. The diagnoses are documented conditions of the
% record (the shared template "the medical record of B documents C"):
% cystic fibrosis, bronchiectasis, or a condition of the LCD's neuromuscular
% list (the knowledge base facts below). What characterizes the
% bronchiectasis is a fact of the record with its number — the months of
% daily productive cough (the threshold, 6, is in the rule), the
% exacerbations requiring antibiotic therapy in a year (more than 2) — and
% so is the CT confirmation. Chronic bronchitis and COPD, the LCD says, do
% not meet criterion 2 without a confirmed bronchiectasis: they are simply
% not among the conditions the rules read. Criterion 4 is one clinical
% judgment, the judged template of dmepos.le "the finding F about B is
% established" (or unsupported), with who found it and why:
%   standard treatments failed to mobilize secretions (criterion 4: the
%   well-documented failure of standard treatments — chest physiotherapy,
%   postural drainage, medications, other modalities — to adequately
%   mobilize retained secretions).
% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table (sources/icd10/A52494_icd10_covered.csv,
% one group, serving E0483, A7025 and A7026) is data, loaded as the table
% hfcwo_icd10; it is read by the payment condition the Article adds: the
% diagnosis code that justifies the need must be on the claim (section
% remedy). The record's conditions decide the coverage question; the
% claim's code its documentation.
%
% Not modelled: the KX/GA/GZ modifiers (billing); the coding guidelines
% (A7025 and A7026 billed with E0483 is unbundling, a matter of coding).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the bronchiectasis of *a beneficiary* was confirmed by a CT scan; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has had a daily productive cough for *a number* continuous months; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* had *a number* exacerbations requiring antibiotic therapy in the past year; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* uses a mechanical in-exsufflation device; undefined.
    *an item* is used with beneficiary owned equipment; undefined.
    % the knowledge base
    *a condition* is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO.
    % the table
    ICD10 code *a code* is in group *a group* of article *an article* as *a description* under table hfcwo_icd10.
    % derived
    *an item* is a high frequency chest wall oscillation device.
    *an item* is a replacement supply for a high frequency chest wall oscillation device.
    *a beneficiary* meets the HFCWO coverage criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets a diagnosis criterion for HFCWO.
    the bronchiectasis of *a beneficiary* is characterized as HFCWO requires.
    the failure of standard treatments is documented for *a beneficiary*.
    the diagnosis code of *a beneficiary* is a covered HFCWO diagnosis code.

% The Policy Article's ICD-10 table: the covered codes of its one group.
the table hfcwo_icd10 is loaded from sources/icd10/A52494_icd10_covered.csv, with all matches:
    code | group | article | description

the knowledge base hfcwo includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base hfcwo includes:

LCD L33785 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33785".
the text of LCD L33785 is at "sources/lcd/L33785.txt".
Policy Article A52494 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52494".
the text of Policy Article A52494 is at "sources/article/A52494.txt".

% What the device and its replacement supplies are.
rule hfcwo_device with provenance Policy Article A52494,
        confer "HCPCS code E0483 describes a complete system":
an item is a high frequency chest wall oscillation device
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0483".

rule hfcwo_replacement_supply with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "Replacement supplies, A7025 and A7026, used with beneficiary owned equipment, are covered if the beneficiary meets the criteria listed above for the base device, E0483":
an item is a replacement supply for a high frequency chest wall oscillation device
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A7025", "A7026"]
    and the item is used with beneficiary owned equipment.

% The neuromuscular diseases of criterion 3.
post polio syndrome is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Post-polio".
acid maltase deficiency is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Acid maltase deficiency".
anterior horn cell disease is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Anterior horn cell diseases".
multiple sclerosis is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Multiple sclerosis".
quadriplegia is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Quadriplegia".
hereditary muscular dystrophy is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Hereditary muscular dystrophy".
myotonic disorder is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Myotonic disorders".
myopathy is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Other myopathies".
paralysis of the diaphragm is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO,
    as stated in LCD L33785, confer "Paralysis of the diaphragm".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: durable medical
% equipment (Policy Article A52494).
rule hfcwo_codes with provenance Policy Article A52494,
        confer "High frequency chest wall oscillation devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is hfcwo
    if the code is in ["E0483", "A7025", "A7026"].

section applicability is:

rule hfcwo_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52494,
        confer "High frequency chest wall oscillation devices are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is hfcwo.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The device, and the replacement supplies of a beneficiary owned device:
% covered when the beneficiary meets the criteria.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule hfcwo_covered with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "High frequency chest wall oscillation devices (HFCWO) (E0483) are covered for beneficiaries who meet":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a high frequency chest wall oscillation device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the HFCWO coverage criteria.

rule hfcwo_supplies_covered with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "Replacement supplies, A7025 and A7026, used with beneficiary owned equipment, are covered if the beneficiary meets the criteria listed above for the base device, E0483":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a replacement supply for a high frequency chest wall oscillation device
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the HFCWO coverage criteria.

% The criteria: 1, 2 or 3, and 4; and not both devices.
rule hfcwo_criteria with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "Criterion 1, 2, or 3, and Criterion 4":
a beneficiary meets the HFCWO coverage criteria
    if the beneficiary meets a diagnosis criterion for HFCWO
    and the failure of standard treatments is documented for the beneficiary
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary uses a mechanical in-exsufflation device.

% Criterion 1: cystic fibrosis.
rule hfcwo_criterion_1 with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "There is a diagnosis of cystic fibrosis":
a beneficiary meets a diagnosis criterion for HFCWO
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents cystic fibrosis.

% Criterion 2: bronchiectasis confirmed by a CT scan and characterized by
% the cough or the exacerbations.
rule hfcwo_criterion_2 with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "which has been confirmed by a high resolution, spiral, or standard CT scan and which is characterized by":
a beneficiary meets a diagnosis criterion for HFCWO
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents bronchiectasis
    and the bronchiectasis of the beneficiary was confirmed by a CT scan
    and the bronchiectasis of the beneficiary is characterized as HFCWO requires.

rule hfcwo_daily_cough with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "Daily productive cough for at least 6 continuous months":
the bronchiectasis of a beneficiary is characterized as HFCWO requires
    if the beneficiary has had a daily productive cough for a number continuous months
    and the number >= 6.

rule hfcwo_exacerbations with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "Frequent (i.e., more than 2/year) exacerbations requiring antibiotic therapy":
the bronchiectasis of a beneficiary is characterized as HFCWO requires
    if the beneficiary had a number exacerbations requiring antibiotic therapy in the past year
    and the number > 2.

% Criterion 3: a neuromuscular disease of the list.
rule hfcwo_criterion_3 with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "The beneficiary has one of the following neuromuscular disease diagnoses":
a beneficiary meets a diagnosis criterion for HFCWO
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a qualifying neuromuscular disease for HFCWO.

% Criterion 4: the finding.
rule hfcwo_criterion_4 with provenance LCD L33785,
        confer "There must be well-documented failure of standard treatments to adequately mobilize retained secretions":
the failure of standard treatments is documented for a beneficiary
    if the finding standard treatments failed to mobilize secretions about the beneficiary is established.

% "It is not reasonable and necessary for a beneficiary to use both a HFCWO
% device and a mechanical in-exsufflation device (E0482)": the negation in
% the criteria rule.

section remedy is:

% The Policy Article's own condition of payment: the diagnosis code that
% justifies the need, on the claim — a code of the Article's ICD-10 list.
rule hfcwo_diagnosis_code_on_claim with provenance Policy Article A52494,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on the claim":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is hfcwo
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a covered HFCWO diagnosis code.

rule hfcwo_covered_diagnosis_code with provenance Policy Article A52494,
        confer "The diagnosis code that justifies the need for these items must be included on the claim":
the diagnosis code of a beneficiary is a covered HFCWO diagnosis code
    if the diagnosis code of the beneficiary is a code
    and ICD10 code the code is in group 1 of article "A52494" as a description under table hfcwo_icd10.
